{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S6 (0d76-ebbf-ee3a-48ac) PARITY VERDICT, carried to this epic as a COMMENT rather than a\ndescription edit — a description edit would be material and would invalidate this epic's\nplan-review attestation at the worst point in the sequence (the epic closes last).\n\nBEDROCK DID NOT CLEAR THE PARITY BAR. Both class slots were measured live in\n896586841071/us-east-1 (30-item pooled gold corpus, 28 scored, N=3 epochs, 360 case-runs,\n~15.4M input tokens):\n\n  standard  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6  FAILED — 1 decision-level flip (bar: 0)\n  frontier  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8    FAILED — 2 flips, agreement 0.929 < 0.95,\n                                                     and the false-accept criterion\n\nSo the epic's \"first-class provider\" tier label for Bedrock is NOT earned by measurement today,\nand S8 (eb6e) must not cut the production review bot over citing a cleared bar.\n\nTHE NUANCE MATTERS AND SHOULD NOT BE LOST: all three flips run in Bedrock's FAVOUR against the\ngold labels — on standard it caught a gold-BLOCK case direct Anthropic missed (recall 0.857 ->\n0.929), and on frontier it correctly declined to fire on two gold-ADVISORY cases direct\nAnthropic false-fired on. Validity was 1.000 on both arms of both slots over 360 case-runs,\nruntime error rate 0.000, latency at or better than direct Anthropic, and the v2 arms were\nprovably provider-clean (zero non-Bedrock calls). The failure is specifically the\n\"zero decision-level flips\" criterion, not a quality regression.\n\nBefore Bedrock's first-class claim is re-litigated, the S6 comment thread recommends three\nthings in order: land 635f (the missing `errored` guard, which did not affect this run but would\nfabricate flips on a flakier one); settle whether `parity._recall_false_accept` is inverted (it\ncomputes specificity and the gate fails when it RISES, which is what failed the frontier slot);\nand run the SAME harness Anthropic-vs-Anthropic to establish the bar's own noise floor at N=3 on\na 28-item gold set — the control this run lacks. If a same-provider run also flips, the problem\nis the bar, and changing it is a deliberate decision for this epic, not something S6 may assume.\n\nFull numbers, per-criterion breakdown, run provenance and the committed artifact\n(`src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json`, re-scored offline by\n`tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py`) are on 0d76.\n"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785716393610224001,"uuid":"bc649a4d-bc09-4373-86c9-0979ff2124a9"}